        "content": "# Quick Build: Add Json Validation\n\n**Created**: 2026-03-02T00:00:00Z\n**Request**: add a json validation script that's ultra performant\n**Scope**: Small\n\n## Plan\n\n**Reasoning**: This is an additive feature touching 1-3 new files within a single system (the existing Bun/TypeScript project). No existing code needs modification. Risk is low since this is a new, self-contained module. Estimated effort is under 2 hours.\n\n**Files Affected**:\n- `src/validate-json.ts` (new -- core validation module)\n- `src/validate-json.test.ts` (new -- tests)\n- `src/index.ts` (minor update to re-export or wire in CLI entry)\n\n**Approach**: Create a high-performance JSON validation module using a compile-once, validate-many pattern. The validator will accept a JSON schema definition (supporting common types: string, number, boolean, object, array, with nested properties and required fields) and compile it into a reusable validation function that avoids repeated schema traversal. This avoids heavy dependencies by hand-rolling a focused validator optimized for the hot path: type checking, required-field presence, and property validation using pre-built lookup maps. The Bun runtime's native performance characteristics will be leveraged. Comprehensive tests will cover valid/invalid payloads, edge cases (empty objects, nested schemas, arrays), and performance assertions.\n\n**Estimated Effort**: 1.5 hours\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Create `src/validate-json.ts` with TypeScript types for schema definition (SchemaType, SchemaProperty, ValidationResult) and a `compileValidator(schema)` function that returns a reusable `(data: unknown) => ValidationResult` closure with pre-computed required-field sets and type-check maps `[complexity:medium]`\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement core validation logic inside the compiled closure -- type checking (string, number, boolean, object, array), required-field enforcement, nested object recursion, and array item validation, all using early-return fast paths and avoiding allocations on the happy path `[complexity:medium]`\n- [ ] **T3**: Create `src/validate-json.test.ts` with tests covering: valid payloads pass, missing required fields fail, wrong types fail, nested object validation, array validation, edge cases (null, undefined, empty objects), and a performance smoke test validating 100k objects under a time threshold `[complexity:medium]`\n- [ ] **T4**: Export the validator from `src/index.ts` and add a `validate` script entry in `package.json` for CLI usage (e.g., `bun run validate <schema.json> <data.json>`) `[complexity:simple]`\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n{To be added by task-builder}\n\n## Verification\n\n{To be added by task-reviewer if --review flag used}\n"
